(6301006, 933238, 124815, '<td valign="top">This image becomes very humorous once one reads its title. But:<br/> <br/>I experience more and more saturation with these type of photos, as interesting or beautiful as they are, they tend to be "post Gerhard Richter". <br/>Perhaps a better place for them would be in a different kind of challenge, with a pure bend towards mixed media. In which case they would get the proper consideration. <br/>This is by no means a criticism to this particular image but to a trend that I saw for the month and a half that I am on this site, therefore, in all fairness, I will copy and paste this comment to all related photos.<br/>Please do not consider me rude or with primitive tastes. I just want to do justice, at least in my mind, to each image and appreciate it for its uniqueness in the context in which it is presented.</td>', 'This image becomes very humorous once one reads its title. But: I experience more and more saturation with these type of photos, as interesting or beautiful as they are, they tend to be "post Gerhard Richter". Perhaps a better place for them would be in a different kind of challenge, with a pure bend towards mixed media. In which case they would get the proper consideration. This is by no means a criticism to this particular image but to a trend that I saw for the month and a half that I am on this site, therefore, in all fairness, I will copy and paste this comment to all related photos.Please do not consider me rude or with primitive tastes. I just want to do justice, at least in my mind, to each image and appreciate it for its uniqueness in the context in which it is presented.', '2011-02-02 10:45:54.000000', NULL, 1),
